diag(min8): keep the early framebuffer drawing alive after TTBR0 goes (kernel VA alias) and add blocks 20-27

0340/0341 reached block 19 (just before set_mmu_ttb(invalid_ttep)); the reset is after TTBR0 is turned off, where the PA alias of the DECON framebuffer disappears. Map the 32 MiB block holding the scanout buffer at the empty kernel VA above the low globals in the final table (as the donor's sweet_early_map_final()), relocate the early drawing pointer there after TTBR1 is final (no more sweet_early_disable() before the TTBR0 switch; it still happens at serial_init), and draw blocks 20-27: after TTBR0 off / TLB flush (20), table pointers rebound (21), before pmap_bootstrap (22), after it (23), early I/O tables ready (24), arm_vm_init returned (25), before serial_init (26), after serial_init (27). herostop=N works for the new slots.

